WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.389
When, in 2007 (mistake in the video, I said 2017*), I met my ex French girlfriend in a hostel

00:00:03.389 --> 00:00:06.690
in Prague, I would have never imagined that French

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.269
would become such an important part of my life.

00:00:09.269 --> 00:00:12.809
Hi, my name is Luca from LucaLampariello.doc and today

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:17.010
I would like to talk to you about how I have learned French and the lessons

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:24.600
I have learned on the way. I am positive about it now, but

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.170
I didn't know it back then when I started learning French in highschool some 20 years ago -

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:32.460
what counts the most in language learning is not what you do in the class,

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.600
but what you do OUTSIDE of it, and that's exactly what I started doing

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.489
2 years later, when I started learning French in highschool.

00:00:41.489 --> 00:00:44.160
I started watching French TV all the time. I had discovered

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.930
that I could actually watch France 2, and not just the spoken language -

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:53.550
I could watch everything with subtitles - Page 888 - I still remember that

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.289
and I remember that that gave me a lot of enthusiasm

00:00:58.289 --> 00:01:02.760
and I started watching TV-series, documentaries,movies

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:08.520
every single night, and taking notes since I could actually see the words

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:13.320
that I was hearing. That alone completely changed my approach and perspective on learning French

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:17.070
and when you learn a language at school or in a class

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:19.439
in a language school,

00:01:19.439 --> 00:01:25.590
you have to know that what you do outside of that class counts for 90 %

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:29.909
of your language learning process. If you work outside, what you do at school

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:34.310
is literally the "icing on the cake".

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:40.970
Si ton tonton tond mon tonton, ton tonton sera tondu" French is a language

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:45.710
where nothing is as it seems. Actually, the spoken language

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:49.310
is quite different from the written language, and that's also why the "dictéee" is considered

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:53.479
an indispensable and compulsory tool to master the French language.

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:57.470
I still remember very well when I used to attend high school that

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:02.000
one of our schoolmates was French - he had moved to Rome with his family.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.259
He spoke perfect French, but he had a really hard time writing it.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:10.160
It is important to keep in mind that when you learn a language,

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:15.769
you have to learn it holistically, globally, that is,

00:02:15.769 --> 00:02:21.650
speaking it well means also to learn to read and write, and the abilities that you develop over the years

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:25.640
are going to mutually reinforce each other. That's a really important point

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:29.800
that you should not forget, and you should make sure you tackle all aspects of a given language

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:34.600
every day or over the course of a week.

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:39.060
As I said at the beginning of the video, when I met my ex French gilfriend,

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:42.330
I would have never imagined that French would become such an important part of my life,

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:46.620
I would have never imagined that I would move to France. This has changed and

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.530
broadened my perspective on language learning in general,

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:52.680
because when I used to live in France, I have discovered that

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:57.510
speaking a language is also about knowing the culture, and I have seen .. well, I already knew it,

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:01.410
but I actually witnessed it with my very own eyes - that living there every day

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:06.150
is a different ball game, you learn experience things such when you open the "galette des rois",

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:11.340
the gestures that the French make, cultural references,

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:14.310
things you can or can't do in a given country,

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:17.400
like for example the fact that cutting the salad is a perfectly normal thing to do in Italy, a bit less

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:23.100
in France and all this has given me a brighter perspective on

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.220
what it means to learn a foreign language. I say all the time that

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:31.500
learning a language is doable in your own country - but

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:36.720
if you really want to reach a native-like level in your target language - it is important to live that language

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:42.180
and live in a given country, it will give you a global perspective

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:47.220
on that linguistic system because once again, a language is also its culture, and its culture is also

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:53.549
that language, you should never forget that. Ok, we got tot the end of the video

00:03:53.549 --> 00:03:56.790
and to wrap up: it is very important

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:01.440
to learn outside of the class, that counts for 90 % of your

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.410
learning process. It is very important to learn a given language

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:08.940
in a global way, because a language is like a living organism, and third

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:13.019
it is important - if you want to reach a native-like level in that language - to live

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:18.030
in-country because you are going to witness how people actually live and breathe their own language.

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.340
If you want to know more, you can click on the link in the

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:24.300
description box - I have written an extensive article in English on the marvellous French language

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:28.060
which you can also listen to in English.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:32.260
You are more than welcome to my website and my blog, thanks of listeining

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:45.149
and I'll see you soon here on YouTube!

